% n26_numtype_not_a_type -- the nomination is CHECKED, not trusted. `v : I64`
% is a VALUE, so `numtype v` is refused (kernel 33) even though I64 is itself
% a type. Without this rule any constant could be nominated.
0 sort 0
axiom I64 : 0
1 const I64
axiom v : 1
numtype v
2 const I64
3 sort 0
4 pi 2 3
axiom P : 4
5 const P
6 num 7
7 app 5 6
8 sort 0
check 7 : 8
